Image processing pipeline:

1. Authenticate the user.
2. Validate the file.
3. Check actual file signature and MIME type.
4. Apply size and dimension restrictions.
5. Decode the image safely.
6. Strip unnecessary metadata.
7. Generate a preview.
8. Store the image privately.
9. Run optional image preprocessing.
10. Extract visible chart labels.
11. Pass the image to a vision-capable provider.
12. Generate structured observations.
13. Validate extracted information.
14. Persist the processing result.
15. Return status to the frontend.

Do not execute uploaded content.

Reject unsafe file types.

Prevent decompression bombs, malformed image attacks, storage abuse, and path traversal.

Use private storage and short-lived signed URLs.

Support cancellation and retry where technically feasible.

